Recommends: berigna-nautilus,
 libccid,
 opensc-pkcs11
Description: sign and verify documents with the Peruvian DNIe
 berigna signs and verifies documents with the certificates of the
 Peruvian electronic identity card (DNIe), read from a smart card
 reader: PAdES for PDF, CAdES and XAdES for other files, from the
 basic signature (B-B) to the long-term archival signature (B-LTA),
 with a timestamp from an IOFE accredited authority.
 .
 It verifies signed documents with the ETSI indications, signs batches
 of documents with a single PIN, draws a visible signature and writes
 verification reports in JSON and PDF. The interface is in Peruvian
 Spanish and Southern Quechua. Free software (GPL-3.0-or-later).
 .
 The card is accessed through a dedicated APDU driver over PC/SC
 (ADR-0012): the private key never leaves the card.

Package: berigna-nautilus
Architecture: all
# ${python3:Depends} is required: dh_python3 only acts on packages that list it
# (BRG-DSP-001 §8); the private-dir call in debian/rules byte-compiles the
# extension and guesses its dependencies (python3-gi, already pulled by
# python3-nautilus).
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 berigna (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-nautilus
Description: Nautilus extension to sign and verify with berigna
 "Firmar con berigna" and "Verificar firma" in the context menu of
 Nautilus (GNOME Files): the selected files open in berigna, which
 reads the Peruvian DNIe and signs or verifies them. Several files, or
 a folder, open the batch mode.
 .
 The extension launches berigna with the selection and never reads the
 files itself; the running instance receives them through D-Bus
 (RF-070, RF-073).
